lens:
Mobile UX, accessibility and web performance, round 6. I tested as a 360x640 Android shopper in the Instagram in-app browser, and also at 390x844, 360x600, 360x560, 320x568, 390x664, 393x760, 412x732 and 412x915.

Stress cases:
- bottom safe-area insets of 0 and 34 px (CDP Emulation.setSafeAreaInsetsOverride);
- Android Font size at 115%, 130%, 150% and 200%. This round the nine --t-* tokens are scaled IN THE HTML before any script runs, as WebView textZoom does, so tight mode and the --bar ResizeObserver see the scaled page from the first layout;
- Android fallback faces (Roboto and Noto Serif) for the throttled runs.

G3 holds. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-5.jpg and measure.json (06:59:17-21) are newer than prototype.html (06:58:55, md5 74dcaeee). My renders of an untouched copy match them: facts end at 562, the bar starts at 575, no console errors. fold.png is md5-identical to round 5 (d4ae18d6), and fold-ad.png equals it by design.

All six of my round-5 P1/P2 fixes landed and measure as intended:
- the min-height column: the facts never overlap the next section;
- scroll restoration: Back from a set piece's page returns to 739;
- every scripted jump owns a history entry: Read the policy 2925 -> Back 300; See the set 739 -> Back 0;
- Size guide opens the ruler in the viewer, and Back returns to 1953 with focus on Size guide (real tap);
- tight mode;
- the dock tests #product-facts;
- the viewer pages with the arrow keys (3 / 7, '3 of 7' announced; Escape returns focus to #track);
- the bar grows at 150-200%.

Two round-5 changes cost something:
(1) The tall-screen 3:4 hero is a 172 KB JPEG at about q90. On 390x844 at DPR 3 and 412x915 it moves LCP from about 1.22 s to 1.80 s.
(2) Tight mode measures innerHeight minus 65 px. It ignores the bottom inset and the live --bar, so with a 34 px inset at 115% it stays off while COD sits 18-20 px under the bar.

New finding: the bag's in-place policy disclosure opens below the bag's fixed foot. Only 12 of its 117 px show at 360x640 (36 of 98 at 390x664), so the tap looks dead and leaves a half-cut line.

Probes ran over http://127.0.0.1 against an untouched copy. Speed used CDP throttling (150 ms RTT, 1.6 Mbps, 4x CPU) at DPR 2, 2.625 and 3. Fixes 1-5 were built into a separate copy, /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r6/proto/variant6.html (mkvar6.py), and checked there:
- its first screen is md5-identical to the prototype at 360x640, 320x568, 412x732, 360x560 and 390x664;
- axe finds 0 violations in all 9 states;
- clicking all 57 controls three times raises no JS error.
The prototype was not edited.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r6/out:
- folds_prototype.json, folds_variant6.json, cmp_r6_largetext.jpg, fold390x844_prototype.png and fold390x844_variant6.png;
- perf.json and perf_variant.json;
- hist6.json, ax6.json, bagpol_*.png, cmp_bagpol.jpg, end_360.png, size_viewer.png, land_riya.png, live_bench_proto.jpg and clip_strip.jpg.
The scripts are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/ux_r6: fold6.js, perf6.js, hist6.js, tapfocus.js, bagpol6.js, ax6.js, contrast6.js, docksweep.js, layout6.js, swipe6.js, same6.js, diff6.js, pinch6.js, monkey.js and mkvar6.py.

score_now is the weighted mean of C1, C2, C12, C13, C14, C15, C16 and C20, the same set as rounds 2-5: 396.6 / 44 = 9.01, reported as 9.0. The critique is also written to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/pdp10/rounds/r6_ux.json.

criteria.note:
At the design target every item fits on one line:
- the worn hero at 77-387;
- the H1 at 399-427;
- the price with GST and 'Surgical steel, PVD rhodium';
- the ladder at ₹2,159 / ₹1,919 / ₹1,679;
- 'Free insured delivery, est. 18–20 Nov · COD available' ending at 562;
- the bar at 575 (measure.json, fold.png).

The fact line ends 13 px clear at 360x640, 390x844, 360x600, 360x560, 320x568, 390x664, 393x760 and 412x732, with and without a 34 px inset. At 412x915 it is 48 px clear. No viewport scrolls sideways at any text size.

Round 5's tight mode fixed what it set out to fix:
- 360x560 at 115%: 13 px clear (was 26 under);
- 360x640 at 130%: 13 px clear.

Gaps (folds_prototype.json):
(a) Tight mode ignores the bottom inset. With 34 px it stays off and COD sits under the bar: 360x600 at 115% by 20 px, 320x568 at 115% by 18 px, and 360x560 at 115% by 10 px.
(b) At 150% on 360x640, COD is 46 px under the bar, and 80 px with the inset.
(c) 390x844 at 200% with the inset: 26 px under.
Fix 2 brings (a) to 13/2/12 px clear, (b) to 5 px clear (29 px under with the inset) and (c) to 13 px clear. No default-size first screen changes (folds_variant6.json, same6.js).

On load the first screen is clean:
- no popup, timer or overlay at any time;
- the chip and its inline thumbnail paint with the facts;
- the worn frame shows its own 451-byte placeholder until the hero lands;
- '1 / 7' is quiet.
Round 5's min-height column removed the text-on-text overlap at every size and in landscape (overlap 0 in all 90 matrix cases).

Remaining, at large text only (cmp_r6_largetext.jpg):
- at 150% on 360x640, the delivery and COD line is half-cut by the bar's top edge, which is C2's own fail condition;
- at 130% on 360x600 the line runs 1 px under the bar;
- when the photo is at its 180 px floor, object-position 50% 100% cuts the top of the bracelet, so the stones leave the frame on the left.
Fix 2's caption step and 'object-position: 50% 72%' in tight mode keep the whole bracelet in the band and put the line above the bar (panels 2 and 4).

fixes.change:
Measure tight mode against the column itself, re-check it when the bar changes, and add a second step.
(a) Script:
var f = document.getElementById('product-facts'), r = document.documentElement, ab = f.parentNode;
var fit = window.__fit = function () { r.classList.remove('nf-tight', 'nf-tight2'); var col = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(ab).minHeight); if (f.offsetHeight + 180 > col) { r.classList.add('nf-tight'); if (f.offsetHeight + 180 > col) r.classList.add('nf-tight2'); } };
getComputedStyle(.above).minHeight resolves to px ('509px' at 390x664). It already includes the live --bar and env(safe-area-inset-bottom), and uses svh, so it does not flicker as a browser bar collapses.
(b) In barH(): if (h) { document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--bar', Math.ceil(h + 17) + 'px'); if (window.__fit) window.__fit(); }
(c) CSS:
.nf-tight2 .lk { display: none; }
.nf-tight .sl.worn img { object-position: 50% 72%; }
Only at 150% and up does the ladder caption go; the rung labels still say '2 pieces · 10% off'. On a short band the frame centres on the bracelet instead of cutting its top.

Measured on variant6 (folds_variant6.json, cmp_r6_largetext.jpg), the fact line now ends:
- 360x600 at 115%, 34 px inset: 13 px clear (was 20 under);
- 320x568 at 115% + 34: 2 clear (was 18 under);
- 360x560 at 115% + 34: 12 clear (was 10 under);
- 360x600 at 130%: 13 clear (was 1 under);
- 360x640 at 150%: 5 clear (was 46 under);
- 390x844 at 200% + 34: 13 clear (was 26 under);
- 390x664 at 150% + 34: 13 clear (was 13 under).
Every default-size first screen is md5-identical (same6.js).

In the budget test, add 360x600 at 1.15 with a 34 px inset, and 360x640 at 1.5.

Keep 8 px between neighbouring targets where links wrap:
- footer nav { column-gap: 24px; row-gap: 8px; }
- .rvlinks { row-gap: 8px; }
- .assure .ask .links { row-gap: 8px; }

The footer still holds two rows at 360 ('Contact & business address' and 'Faulty-piece policy', then 'Privacy' and 'Terms'). Its hit areas are now 10 px apart side by side (were 6) and 8 px between rows (were 0). WhatsApp and Business address under Reviews are now 8 px apart (were 0). The ax6.js census on variant6 finds no pair under 8 px apart outside the fold rows.
